    "body": "Back to draft (orchestrating session): a finding from the work on #864, which is stacked on this branch.\n\n`crates/app/src/geometry/import/step.rs` about line 207 compares the chord target with `MAX_CHORD` (0.005) in the FILE's own units, before the conversion to mm. For an inch STEP file the cap is therefore 0.005 in = 0.127 mm, even when the model fits the facet budget - 25 times coarser than this PR intends, so the convex-wall risk this PR closes for mm models stays open for inch models, and an inch bore at its own size can still be read as a gouge.\n\nExpected fix: the target is capped at `MAX_CHORD / mm_per_unit` (i.e. 0.005 mm expressed in the file's unit), with a pinning test on an inch STEP (the chord error of the kept mesh, converted to mm, is at most the cap; and the bore-at-its-own-size case posts clean on an inch model). To be verified and fixed by the PR's author before the high-tier review.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
